# Watchers: Do Something on Change

While computed properties are great for deriving data, sometimes you need to **perform side effects** when data changes – like making an API call, logging, or updating the DOM.

Vue provides **watchers** for this:

```javascript
watch: {
  searchTerm(newVal, oldVal) {
    console.log('Search term changed from', oldVal, 'to', newVal);
    this.fetchResults(newVal);
  }
}
```

Watchers let you react to changes in any reactive property (data, computed, props).

You can watch a property by defining a function with the same name inside the `watch` option:

```javascript
export default {
  data() {
    return { count: 0 };
  },
  watch: {
    // This function runs whenever count changes
    count(newVal, oldVal) {
      console.log(`Count changed from ${oldVal} to ${newVal}`);
    }
  }
}
```

You can also watch nested properties using dot notation: `'obj.property'(newVal, oldVal) { ... }`.
